{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>In the fear of YHWH</b> [there is] strong confidence — two [words] joined. And the bet serves for both at the head of the verse, and likewise the interpretation: on account of the fear of YHWH, HaShem will be a stronghold of strength for the one who fears, to take refuge in Him in the time of his trouble." "<b>And his children</b> — by his merit HaShem will be a refuge of strength." "<b>And the fear of YHWH is a fountain of life</b> — as though the fear is a fountain of life for the one who fears, because he will turn aside from the snares of death, which are transgressions."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "Resolved השם as HaShem (divine name) rather than 'the name,' consistent with Ibn Ezra's usage throughout."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:50.547585135Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}